data/raw/*
data/processed/*
outputs/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
# Frozen historical seed data (see root .gitignore for why these are tracked).
!data/raw/player_stats_2021_2025.rds
!data/raw/team_games.rds
!data/raw/schedules.rds
!data/processed/game_features.rds
!data/processed/td_game_context.rds
!data/processed/td_deployment_model.rds
# De-vig hold-by-price-band table (scripts/146) and the drive-concentration
# recalibration coefficients (scripts/117) -- both frozen, one-time-fitted
# artifacts with no CI step that rebuilds them. Without these tracked, the
# live board silently degrades to no-de-vig / no-recalibration (both paths
# have a graceful fallback) rather than failing loudly, so this is easy to
# miss - added 2026-10-13 alongside the TD model resync.
!data/processed/td_devig_hold_table.rds
!data/processed/td_drive_concentration_calibrator.rds
# Redzone/xTD features (scripts/73_td_redzone_features.R) - a HARD dependency
# of join_td_redzone_features() (R/touchdown_registry.R: stop()s if missing,
# unlike the graceful-fallback artifacts above). Meant to be refreshed WEEKLY
# from fresh play-by-play, not frozen - tracked as a bootstrap copy so the
# very first CI run (before any scheduled refresh has happened) still has it;
# nfl.yml's publish-spread-total/publish-full jobs refresh it for real.
!data/processed/td_redzone_features.rds
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!outputs/.gitkeep

# These reports live under outputs/ but are hand-written source documents, not
# build artifacts. No script regenerates them, so they must be tracked or the
# frozen 2026 rules and their rationale would exist only on one disk.
!outputs/analysis_report.md
!outputs/2026_betting_plan.md
!outputs/touchdown_model_report.md
!outputs/touchdown_prop_model_plan.md
!outputs/td_2026_operating_plan.md
!outputs/fantasy_prop_model_report.md
!outputs/percentage_interaction_report.md
!outputs/player_prop_backtest_report.md
!outputs/model_upgrade_report.md
!outputs/preseason_draft_analysis.md
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
.Rlib/
config/secrets.yml
.env
!outputs/draft_model_report.md
